-- title:
--   Division-value functions on the Tate curve and diamond permutation
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $M$ a natural number with $2 \le M$, and $\zeta \in K$ a primitive $M$-th root of unity. Write $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH M ⊥)` for the intermediate field of $K((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries K` over $K$ generated by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ on the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of the $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose image under [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units M`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) (the unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ given by the lower-right entry) is trivial, $p_f,p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ are power series whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ are the $q$-expansions at $\infty$ of $f$ and $g$, and the coefficientwise reduction of $p_g$ to $K$ is non-zero. The assertion is that there are two families $w_1, w_2 \colon (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to F$ with the following three properties. First, for every $t$ the Laurent series underlying $w_1(t)$ is $c_4\,(1 + 12 X_t)/c_6$, where $c_4, c_6$ are the invariants of the Tate curve `tateLaurent K` over $K((q))$ (the base change of $\langle 1,0,0,a_4,a_6\rangle$ over $\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$) and $X_t$ is the first component of `toricPoint K 1 (ζ ^ (t : ZMod M).val)`, i.e. the series with constant term $c/(1-c)^2$ and $m$-th coefficient $\sum_{d \mid m} (m/d)(c^{m/d} + c^{-m/d}) - 2\sigma_1(m)$ for $c = \zeta^{t}$. Secondly, the Laurent series underlying $w_2(t)$ is $(X_t + 6X_t^2 + 2a_4)/c_4$. Thirdly, for every monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\Gamma_0(M)$ to the group of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $F$ satisfying `IsDiamondPullbackModL K M ⊥ ρ` — that is, $\rho(\gamma)$ carries any element whose Laurent series is $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_{f_1})/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_{g_1})$ to $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$ whenever $f_1 = f\mid_k \gamma$ and $g_1 = g\mid_k \gamma$ for forms of weight $k$ on that subgroup with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g) \neq 0$ — one has $\rho(\gamma)(w_i(t)) = w_i\bigl(t \cdot (\mathrm{gamma0Units}\,M\,\gamma)^{-1}\bigr)$ for $i = 1,2$, all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ and all $t \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$.
--
--   The two families are the level-$M$ division-value (Weber-type) functions attached to the $M$-torsion point $\zeta^t$ of the Tate curve, realised as ratios of integral $q$-expansions of forms of weight $2$ and $4$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$; the third clause records that any automorphism action of $\Gamma_0(M)$ of diamond type permutes them by $t \mapsto t d^{-1}$, where $d$ is the lower-right entry modulo $M$. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.exists_algHom_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_bot_comp_eq_iff_and_comp_diamondPullbackModL_of_transcendental_j`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_algHom_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH_bot_comp_eq_iff_and_comp_diamondPullbackModL_of_transcendental_j), where these functions serve as explicit generators on which embeddings of the $q$-expansion function field and the diamond action are tested.
